{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgujiHLagqF3nba3Ajj11","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No new defects, and no code in the milestone changed since the previous round. The two earlier low-severity findings are still present and unchanged.\n\n**decision: approved**\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **What changed since round 5 (aa575b36 → 9a4878e7):** `git diff --stat` shows that the only edit inside this milestone is one sentence in `.pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md:20`. It says the roadmap review is made on this frozen commit. None of the runtime code, the runtime tests, the resident memo or the ADR changed. The other changes in the range are elsewhere in the engine: `check.go`, `review_dispatch.go`, two new tests for them, indexes and review records. The sealed `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` and `integration:pose-mcp/go/check-index-generation-integration` results cover them.\n- **R3-N4 (not fixed):** `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:280` still runs the heavy `review-check` alongside the short queries and throws away its output and where it ran (`via`). The T5 verdict at `:378` still says every hosted run matched the standalone output. S6 (`:306`) does compare two heavy runs to the standalone output, which limits the gap. Low; stays a follow-up.\n- **R3-N5 (not fixed):** At a deadline, `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:160-161` still adds one to `busy` while the connection is still counted in `inflight`. The connection only leaves the count once the reply is written (`pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go:369`). In that short window the status's in-flight count (`runtime.go:503`) and the stop's `Drained` count (`runtime.go:472-486`) can read one too high. Low; stays a follow-up.\n- **Membership:** all three member specs are `status: done`:\n  - `.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md:3`\n  - `.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md:3`\n  - `.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement.md:3`\n- **Exit gate:**\n  - **Measurements:** the fourth run in `.pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.json:433-439` passes T1–T7.\n  - **Identity:** a hosted request is checked against the runtime's identity before any handler runs (`runtime.go:449-456`).\n  - **Protected endpoint:** the peer's user ID is checked before any byte is read (`runtime.go:404-408`).\n  - **Departures:** the roadmap at `:74` and the ADR's last amendment record what was not delivered: CPU quota and affinity, and per-command limits.\n  - **Gate wording:** the \"watcher is a hint\" and \"receipt before retry\" clauses are met indirectly. The memo is keyed by commit (there is no watcher), and a command that may have run is never repeated.\n\n## Limits of this review\n\n- I could not run `go test` or the `pose` tools myself: the profile only allows `git status`/`ls-files` (one early `git log`/`git diff` call did run). Regression and validation rest on the sealed evidence.\n- `closeout-check` and `review-check` can only run once this attestation is recorded, so they are marked deferred.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R3-N4\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:280 still discards the output and via of the concurrent review-check while the T5 verdict at :378 claims every hosted run matched standalone; unchanged since round 5 (git diff --stat aa575b36..HEAD shows no change under pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_*). Low severity; S6 (:306) compares two heavy hosted outputs to standalone, which limits the gap. Remains a low follow-up, as accepted in rounds 4 and 5.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R3-N5\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:160-161 adds busy at the deadline while the connection stays in inflight until the reply is written (pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go:369), so status InFlight (runtime.go:503) and the stop's Drained (runtime.go:472-486) can read one too high for that window. Code unchanged since round 5. Remains a low follow-up, as accepted in rounds 4 and 5.\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Diffed aa575b36..9a4878e7: inside the milestone only .pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md:20 changed (one sentence about reviewing a frozen state); no change to runtime_host.go, runtime_cmd.go, runtime_lanes.go, runtime_measure_test.go, worktreeruntime/*, resident_git_memo*.go or the ADR. Other changes in the range are outside this milestone's specs (cli/check.go, pose/review_dispatch.go and their tests, indexes, review records) and are covered by the sealed unit and check-index-generation evidence. Re-read runtime_host.go:80-166 (admission lanes, deadline, orphan accounting), worktreeruntime/runtime.go:330-504 (accept loop, peer UID check, per-request identity check, idle shutdown, drain, state), runtime_measure_test.go:260-384 (S4-S6, T1-T7), the measurement JSON verdicts (four runs, the fourth passing T1-T7), the roadmap milestone section and exit gate (:63-81) and the status of the three member specs (all done).\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"exit-gate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the B35 exit gate (.pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md:77-81) against the code and the measurement: identity handshake plus a per-request identity check before the handler (worktreeruntime/runtime.go:421-456), peer-UID-protected Unix socket (runtime.go:404-408), lifecycle with stop, drain and idle (runtime.go:375-391, 470-487), and standalone fallback with no rerun after an ambiguous reply (runtime_host.go:168-172). The fourth measurement run passes T1-T7, with RAM, CPU and latency per scenario and two heavy checks at once (measurements.json:433-439). The departures (no watcher, because the memo is keyed by commit; no-rerun in place of a receipt; no CPU quota or per-command limits) are recorded in the ADR amendment and at roadmap :74. Concluded that the gate has falsifiable evidence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"integration\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The three member contracts compose: the endpoint and handshake of pose-optional-worktree-runtime host the typed read checks and the resident memo of pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache, which run in the admission lanes of pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement (runtime_host.go:106-120). Sealed integration evidence passes for all three (optional-worktree-runtime-integration, resident-cache-integration, runtime-qos-integration).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"membership\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The roadmap names three member specs (:67). Each is status: done (.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md:3, 2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md:3, 2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement.md:3), and none of their delivered code changed since their closure and the round-5 approval.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"regression\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Cumulative module validation is sealed as passing: build:pose-mcp/go/build, unit:pose-mcp/go/test and every pose-mcp integration and reachability check listed in the bundle pass, including the checks covering the out-of-milestone changes in this range (check-index-generation-integration, sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration). I could not rerun them in this profile.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"residual-risk\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The cross-spec items not delivered (CPU quota and affinity, per